{"id": "EUVD-2026-86656", "enisaUuid": "b9fadf6c-4271-3305-bc10-5f4e41e518ad", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/amd: Do not reallocate GA log buffers on resume\n\nCommit c5e1a1eb9279 (\"iommu/amd: Simplify and Consolidate Virtual APIC\n(AVIC) Enablement\") moved the GA log allocation from iommu_init_pci()\nto enable_iommus_vapic(), which is called on every resume.\n\niommu_init_ga_log() assigns iommu->ga_log and iommu->ga_log_tail\nunconditionally. Each resume therefore replaces the boot-time pointers\nand leaks both old allocations. The function also uses GFP_KERNEL from a\nsyscore resume callback, where interrupts are disabled and the non-boot\nCPUs are offline.\n\nReturn early if both buffers are already allocated. Clear the pointers\nin free_ga_log() so a partial allocation failure cannot leave ga_log\ndangling.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b95269d7a43b737c2c0e2fa77bf00cc8a3a4434", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff85cdc2889e1c885eed218ee5bc0b59e0235b3f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94458b80d3b203c1c9e2c98aa7319b7713e006c0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6be275d19cee01f8f1f08a2ff18337103d05d40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00a7dd64888d6dd72110b40e2824a088cf7b7386"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98003", "GHSA-mvmg-3rw6-rj84"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03e7cb5e-1954-37d3-92ac-66e59b476eb7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5e1a1eb9279fdb28d47ca2a4493a4c53b7d6a0b <b6be275d19cee01f8f1f08a2ff18337103d05d40"}, {"id": "1b13070c-80b8-373b-9f1b-e4f41e8cc229", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2e7eb224-63a5-3338-bca9-caa6909a65b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3ccadaf8-ea3f-305c-b2ab-ed459cb9dc16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5e1a1eb9279fdb28d47ca2a4493a4c53b7d6a0b <ff85cdc2889e1c885eed218ee5bc0b59e0235b3f"}, {"id": "66181881-ec08-3c04-9f11-46793f41ea8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "a9b7217d-9814-3fd5-957a-54750a073202", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b0200c71-4ee9-392f-8542-1506cdc8046f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5e1a1eb9279fdb28d47ca2a4493a4c53b7d6a0b <94458b80d3b203c1c9e2c98aa7319b7713e006c0"}, {"id": "d02cd108-df8c-3cf5-911b-4c8c5ee7f06f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "d85e4578-6526-3a42-ac85-461cf8a35e54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5e1a1eb9279fdb28d47ca2a4493a4c53b7d6a0b <00a7dd64888d6dd72110b40e2824a088cf7b7386"}, {"id": "de6dcfbc-8249-327b-9b56-0e08f72967b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "e0f101d1-f19c-353a-b489-13577304b7e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5e1a1eb9279fdb28d47ca2a4493a4c53b7d6a0b <8b95269d7a43b737c2c0e2fa77bf00cc8a3a4434"}, {"id": "fb5a1ee0-cf59-33ed-97a8-73bf35599647", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0bd4df32-51aa-3eda-950c-717ff96a47f0", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}